Algorithm

1. Start.
2. Read the number of elements, n.
3. Generate an ascending sequence containing elements from 1 to n.
4. Create a descending sequence by reversing the ascending sequence.
5. Generate a random sequence by shuffling the same elements.
6. Construct three separate BSTs by inserting the elements from each sequence.
7. Calculate each BST's height recursively: return -1 for an empty tree; otherwise return 1 + max(left subtree
height, right subtree height).
8. Display the sequences and their corresponding BST heights.
9. Compare the heights and display the results.
10. Release the allocated memory.
11. Stop.
